      <activity id="dd3d4761-5b6b-5729-a0ab-4caebfe1eb3f" activityNameId="b9100f1d-dada-5f34-9e73-eb28ecd44b80" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, at nuclear power plant, economic allocation</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, at nuclear power plant, economic allocation
Inventory for 1 MJ heat from nuclear power plant. In 2019, of the total energy produced were 97.8% as electricity and 2.2% as heat. The economic factor is 0.72 for ectricity and 0.28 for heat. This leads to the allocation factor of 0.991 for electricity an 0.009 for heat.;
UUID: cff77537-4513-397d-9082-d0feceb42d77
Included is the demnd of materials, energy, infrastructures and transports for the production of heat at a nuclear power plant
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: average technology
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_cff77537-4513-397d-9082-d0feceb42d77.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
